# XF Architecture Model — Cursor Rules
# Full spec: see INSTRUCTIONS.md and CLAUDE.md in this directory.

## Architecture

This project follows the XF Architecture Model (CFAM):
- 3 layers: Access (repository/) → Business (business/) → Interaction (api/)
- 5 types per layer: Logical · Generalization · Injection · Utility · Transfer
- 3 injectors: R (Access) · B (Business) · A (Interaction)
- Dependencies flow DOWNWARD ONLY. No upward or lateral layer calls.

## Mandatory rules

- NEVER call Access (R.*) from Interaction directly — go through Business (B.*).
- NEVER instantiate Logical components with `new`. Use R.x, B.x, A.x.
- NEVER put logic in Transfer objects. Transfers are data-only.
- NEVER put state or I/O in Utility components. Utilities are pure functions.
- ALWAYS register new Logical components in their layer's injector (R, B, or A).
- Init order at startup: R.init() → B.init() → A.init() (via XF.init()). Injections are static, non-instantiable.

## Naming

- Access Logical    → <Concept>Repository   (UserRepository)
- Business Logical  → <Concept>Business     (UserBusiness)
- Interaction/svc   → <Concept>Service      (AuthService)
- Interaction/view  → <Concept>View         (LoginView)
- Generalization    → its layer's logical suffix (Repository/Business/Service/View)
- Utility           → <Concept>Utils        (StringUtils)
- Transfer          → <Concept>             (User, Session)
- Exception         → <Concept>Exception    (Transfer subtype; NetworkException)
- Injection         → R / B / A

## Folders

The four type-subfolder names (general/, logic/, transfers/, utils/) are an
immutable normative contract — use these exact names. The src/ matrix is an
artifact root: it may hang from any path and multiple roots can coexist
(verification runs per root). The entry point (main) lives OUTSIDE the root.

- api/logic/service/   → Interaction Services
- api/logic/gui/       → Interaction Views
- api/general/         → Interaction Generalizations
- api/transfers/       → Interaction Transfers
- api/utils/           → Interaction Utilities
- api/A                → Interaction Injector
- business/logic/      → Business Logicals
- business/general/    → Business Generalizations
- business/transfers/  → Business Transfers
- business/utils/      → Business Utilities
- business/B           → Business Injector
- repository/logic/    → Access Logicals
- repository/general/  → Access Generalizations
- repository/transfers/ → Access Transfers
- repository/utils/    → Access Utilities
- repository/R         → Access Injector

## Before generating any file

1. State the layer and type: "Layer: Business | Type: Logical"
2. Derive name from classification: UserBusiness → business/logic/UserBusiness.ts
3. Verify no layer boundary is crossed in the new file.
4. Update the injector if adding a new Logical.
